      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Also, with the way you currently have it set up, if you have a boot config file but not raw boot config arguments, the genrule will be generated without a command at all.\n\nI think this is highly unlikely, given that there are no existing use cases of `internal_bootconfig_file`.\n\n\u003e Could we instead keep this variable in PartitionVarsForSoongMigrationOnlyDoNotUse and just generate the genrule command with it\u0027s contents hardcoded into it?\n\nWDYT about neverallowing the product variable? Do we really want the content of the product variable to be hardcoded in a generated module? I think that would become an issue when we start to check in the generated bp modules.",
